            ],
            "summary": "Marked the historical LTX-2 profile superseded while retaining its directly deployable immutable execution contract."
          }
        ],
        "prior_recipe_content_sha256": "baff135e07ea79ae4eb19729ee543edd77805a26c9b3922839ab58a63188b2e1",
        "released_at": "2026-09-01",
        "upgrade_effect": "none",
        "version": "2.3.2"
      },
      {
        "changes": [
          {
            "details": "Added codeload.github.com and download-r2.pytorch.org, and removed nvcr.io because verified base images are transferred separately from Dockerfile build egress.",
            "kind": "fix",
            "references": [],
            "summary": "Corrected public build egress for the pinned LTX source archive and PyTorch wheel redirects."
          }
        ],
        "prior_recipe_content_sha256": "32f866c8eb41e0de62f3c18ce9d9ba6107c9c2ca8846402ac45c4cd5e62999a4",
        "released_at": "2026-09-01",
        "upgrade_effect": "rebuild",
        "version": "2.3.1"
      },
      {
        "changes": [
          {
            "details": "The FP4-only adapter now requests disk rather than CPU offload and remains bound exclusively to this recipe. Pinned upstream quantifies disk offload at about 5 GB host RAM plus 5 GB accelerator memory versus about 36 GB host RAM plus 5 GB accelerator memory for CPU offload. The conservative Candidate envelope subtracts only that documented 31 GB host-memory delta: startup 120 to 89 GB and steady 106 to 75 GB, with growth and system reserve unchanged at 8 GB each. Admission therefore requires 97 GB including reserve; physical acceptance remains pending.",
            "kind": "compatibility",
            "references": [
              "https://github.com/Lightricks/LTX-2/blob/a95ab856bf29407b6b066ede0abe1846050db56c/packages/ltx-pipelines/src/ltx_pipelines/utils/types.py",
              "https://github.com/Lightricks/LTX-2/blob/a95ab856bf29407b6b066ede0abe1846050db56c/packages/ltx-pipelines/src/ltx_pipelines/utils/args.py"
            ],
            "summary": "Selected the pinned upstream's explicit disk-streaming offload mode for the LTX-2 19B dev FP4 single-Spark Candidate."
          }
        ],
        "prior_recipe_content_sha256": "06b3a57766d29b92544870a51879b9fc7f22a09784b0402d7f31a9182ce99c03",
        "released_at": "2026-08-31",
        "upgrade_effect": "rebuild",
        "version": "2.3.0"
      },
      {
        "changes": [
          {
            "details": "The adapter fails closed unless ltx-pipelines is version 1.3.0 and PipelineOutput exposes video, audio, num_frames, tiling_config, keyframes, and video_latent.",
            "kind": "runtime",
            "references": [
              "https://github.com/Lightricks/LTX-2/tree/a95ab856bf29407b6b066ede0abe1846050db56c"
            ],
            "summary": "Refreshed the native pipeline from LTX 1.2 to exact 1.3.0 source and its named six-field PipelineOutput contract."
          },
          {
            "details": "The FP4 build now uses the same deterministic archive and dependency-lock path as the other native LTX adapters.",
            "kind": "fix",
            "references": [],
            "summary": "Replaced live Git package resolution with a checksummed source archive and added the required TorchVision and cuDNN 9.24 pins."
          },
          {
            "details": "LTX 1.3 contains DFR and keyframe-aware decode support, but this recipe does not claim those artifact-dependent paths and remains a physical-acceptance Candidate.",
            "kind": "compatibility",
            "references": [],
            "summary": "Kept the declared two-stage interface and conservative memory envelope while inheriting upstream decode-tiling OOM fixes."
          }
        ],
        "prior_recipe_content_sha256": "b458ed9412c5c8036ba79f2210dead04f0843dae56fcf1e6bd1bd4baef6576a5",
        "released_at": "2026-08-31",
        "upgrade_effect": "rebuild",
        "version": "2.2.0"
      },
      {
        "changes": [
          {
            "details": "The checkpoint, distilled LoRA, spatial upscaler, Gemma shards and indexes, and tokenizer closure remain byte-identical. Repository metadata and unrelated checkpoints are no longer downloaded. Gemma now receives the common root containing both text_encoder and tokenizer. The image/build allowance matches the conservative 8 GB envelope used by the same pinned LTX 1.2 runtime family.",
            "kind": "fix",
            "references": [],
            "summary": "Filtered the pinned Hugging Face snapshot to the 25 immutable files required by the native FP4 runtime."
          }
        ],
        "prior_recipe_content_sha256": "bfed18fb1fe5e0768c5c765448038e017c0fe8c1bf5b33a94824c46955cb7868",
        "released_at": "2026-08-29",
        "upgrade_effect": "rebuild",
